1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:18,480
A Place of Our Own

2
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:22,230
I remember your parents' first house very well.

3
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:25,160
It was on Spring Avenue, near the park.

4
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:26,600
I grew up in that house.

5
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:28,850
Yes, and you were such a cute baby.

6
00:00:28,850 --> 00:00:30,870
I've seen pictures of him.

7
00:00:30,870 --> 00:00:32,940
He had blond hair.

8
00:00:32,940 --> 00:00:34,450
I've been friendly with the Stewart family

9
00:00:34,450 --> 00:00:35,160
for a long time,

10
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:36,290
so it's my pleasure

11
00:00:36,290 --> 00:00:37,650
to help you find a house now.

12
00:00:37,650 --> 00:00:39,920
Well, we're not sure we can afford one.

13
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:41,220
But we'd like to find out

14
00:00:41,220 --> 00:00:42,210
about the possibilities.

15
00:00:42,210 --> 00:00:44,220
That's a good idea.

16
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:47,160
I love your house on Linden Street.

17
00:00:47,160 --> 00:00:50,120
I sold your father that house seventeen years ago.

18
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:50,680
Really?

19
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:52,750
Yes, Mom was pregnant with Robbie then,

20
00:00:52,750 --> 00:00:54,340
and they needed the extra room.

21
00:00:54,340 --> 00:00:56,720
I hear you're expecting a baby, Mrs. Stewart.

22
00:00:56,720 --> 00:00:57,320
Mmm-hmm.

23
00:00:57,320 --> 00:00:59,590
So we will be needing more room.

24
00:00:59,590 --> 00:01:01,180
Oh, so you don't need something immediately?

25
00:01:01,180 --> 00:01:03,700
No. But in five or six months ...

26
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:05,710
And time passes so quickly.

27
00:01:05,710 --> 00:01:07,690
Yes, it does.

28
00:01:07,690 --> 00:01:08,600
Well, when you called,

29
00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:10,030
you gave me enough information

30
00:01:10,030 --> 00:01:12,010
about your salaries and your savings.

31
00:01:12,010 --> 00:01:15,070
So I have a good idea about your financial situation.

32
00:01:15,070 --> 00:01:17,350
Let me show you some pictures of houses.

33
00:01:17,350 --> 00:01:19,190
With two bedrooms?

34
00:01:19,190 --> 00:01:21,190
Yes, I think I can show you some.

35
00:01:21,190 --> 00:01:23,290
Of course, they won't be in Riverdale.

36
00:01:23,290 --> 00:01:26,900
The cost of housing's too high for you here.

37
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:29,870
I haven't thought about living anywhere else.

38
00:01:29,870 --> 00:01:32,140
We've always lived in this area.

39
00:01:32,140 --> 00:01:34,480
Where should we look for a house, Mrs. Martinelli?

40
00:01:34,480 --> 00:01:36,400
Well, we have an office in Mount Kisco.

41
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:37,570
It's a lovely area,

42
00:01:37,570 --> 00:01:40,000
and it's only about an hour's drive from here.

43
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:40,860
Here.

44
00:01:40,860 --> 00:01:45,410
I have a book with photos of some homes in that area.

45
00:01:45,410 --> 00:01:51,210
Now, let's see. Here.

46
00:01:51,210 --> 00:01:55,860
This is a lovely two-bedroom house in your price range.

47
00:01:55,860 --> 00:01:59,020
It's pretty,

48
00:01:59,020 --> 00:02:01,060
but I prefer a two-story home.

49
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:02,280
I do, too.

50
00:02:02,280 --> 00:02:04,000
I don't care for a ranch type.

51
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:07,840
OK.

52
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:10,340
Oh, this is a wonderful house.

53
00:02:10,340 --> 00:02:11,280
I know it well.

54
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:12,960
I sold it to the present owners.

55
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:14,680
It looks wonderful.

56
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:16,800
This is a two-bedroom, two-bath house.

57
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:18,390
It has a full basement,

58
00:02:18,390 --> 00:02:20,720
and it is on a half-acre lot.

59
00:02:20,720 --> 00:02:23,630
You can probably afford this one.

60
00:02:23,630 --> 00:02:24,520
I like this house.

61
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:25,840
So do I.

62
00:02:25,840 --> 00:02:27,690
And the price is right.

63
00:02:27,690 --> 00:02:28,700
Would you like to go see it?

64
00:02:28,700 --> 00:02:29,860
Yes. We're planning

65
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:32,250
to talk to someone at the bank next week.

66
00:02:32,250 --> 00:02:34,660
Perhaps we could see the house this weekend.

67
00:02:34,660 --> 00:02:36,100
If someone doesn't buy it before then,

68
00:02:36,100 --> 00:02:40,410
But let's keep looking.

69
00:02:40,410 --> 00:02:42,430
Just to get an idea of some other possibilities.

70
00:02:42,430 --> 00:02:47,130
This is very helpful, Mrs. Martinelli.

71
00:02:47,130 --> 00:02:48,010
Here.

72
00:02:48,010 --> 00:02:51,490
This is a wonderful example of Spanish-style architecture.

73
00:02:51,490 --> 00:02:52,400
Oh,

74
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:55,670
I love the roof tiles on a Spanish-style house.

75
00:02:55,670 --> 00:02:58,780
It looks like the houses in Hollywood.

76
00:02:58,780 --> 00:03:00,040
It's interesting.

77
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:12,830
A house like this in Riverdale costs double the price.

78
00:03:12,830 --> 00:03:15,620
Oh my!

79
00:03:15,620 --> 00:03:18,640
Here's a real buy.

80
00:03:18,640 --> 00:03:19,440
It's a bargain.

81
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:22,140
This house just came on the market.

82
00:03:22,140 --> 00:03:23,060
It's quite lovely.

83
00:03:23,060 --> 00:03:24,820
Is it a two-bedroom house?

84
00:03:24,820 --> 00:03:27,710
No. It has three bedrooms and three baths.

85
00:03:27,710 --> 00:03:29,050
I know the house.

86
00:03:29,050 --> 00:03:30,470
It has a brand new kitchen.

87
00:03:30,470 --> 00:03:33,820
And a living room with a twelve-foot ceiling.

88
00:03:33,820 --> 00:03:35,910
And there's a two-car garage.

89
00:03:35,910 --> 00:03:37,700
Then why don't we go look at this house, too?

90
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:40,030
It's a good investment.

91
00:03:40,030 --> 00:03:41,170
Thank you, Mrs. Martinelli.

92
00:03:41,170 --> 00:03:42,280
Thanks so much.

93
00:03:42,280 --> 00:03:44,050
My pleasure.

94
00:03:44,050 --> 00:03:45,970
Give my best to your parents.

95
00:03:45,970 --> 00:03:48,420
Your father's a wonderful doctor, Richard.

96
00:03:48,420 --> 00:03:50,870
He took care of my daughter

97
00:03:50,870 --> 00:03:53,040
when she was a child.

98
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:53,410
He's the best pediatrician in Westchester.

99
00:03:53,410 --> 00:03:54,250
Thanks, Mrs. Martinelli.

100
00:03:54,250 --> 00:03:55,450
I'll give them your regards.

101
00:03:55,450 --> 00:03:57,980
We really appreciate your advice.

102
00:03:57,980 --> 00:03:59,810
I do think you should go see the houses

103
00:03:59,810 --> 00:04:01,280
and talk to the bank.

104
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:01,870
Here.

105
00:04:01,870 --> 00:04:09,580
Let me give you some information sheets about the houses.

106
00:04:09,580 --> 00:04:12,260
They're both very good buys.

107
00:04:12,260 --> 00:04:14,670
Well, thanks so much for your help and your time,

108
00:04:14,670 --> 00:04:16,180
Mrs. Martinelli.

109
00:04:16,180 --> 00:04:17,720
We've got a lot to talk about.

110
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:20,720
Mmm-hmm. Thanks.
